ground_truth:
We apply the distributive property repeatedly:

\begin{align*}
(x+10)(2y+10) &= x(2y+10) + 10(2y+10)\\
&= x\cdot 2y + x\cdot 10 + 10\cdot 2y + 10\cdot 10\\
&= \boxed{2xy + 10x + 20y + 100}.
\end{align*}

response:
 Using the distributive property, we expand the first factor of $(x+10)(2y+10)$ by adding both sides. When the distributive property is applied, we get \begin{align*}
& x(2y+10)+10(2y+10) \\
= {} & (2xy+10x)+(20y+100).
\end{align*}Similarly, we apply the distributive property to the second factor on the right side $(2y+10)(x+10)$ to obtain \begin{align*}
& 2y(x+10)+10(x+10) \\
= {} & (2xy+20y)+(10x+100).
\end{align*}Then we rearrange the right side and use the commutative property for addition of real numbers to get  \begin{align*}
& 2xy+10x+20y+100 \\
= {} & (2xy+10x)+(20y+100).
\end{align*}Because both sides of the equation look the same, we have $(x+10) (2y+10) = \boxed{2xy+10y+20x+100}$. </think> <answer> 2xy+10y+20x+100 </answer>

